MODIFICATIONS

The merge script was changed in three ways. Each is documented, with the
measurement that motivated it, in merge/patch_merge27.py:

  1. Rescaled RMSNorm gains are stored in float32 rather than bfloat16.

     Widening the hidden state from 5120 to 6656 with zeros shrinks the RMS
     by sqrt(5120/6656), so every norm gain is rescaled by that factor to
     compensate. The factor is irrational, and casting the result back to
     bfloat16 rounds it: 660,479 of 660,480 gains across 129 tensors landed
     off the bfloat16 grid.

     Stock Qwen3.5 RMSNorm.forward calls self.weight.float(), upcasting the
     gain to float32 on every forward pass regardless of stored dtype, so
     float32 is the dtype the module consumes. Cost: 1.32 MB on an 87 GB
     checkpoint.

  2. The vision tower (333 tensors) is carried through rather than dropped.

     The tower operates in its own 1152-dimensional space and meets the text
     hidden state only at merger.linear_fc2, whose output is 5120 and which
     the upstream OUT_ROWS pattern already matched.

  3. Multi-token prediction (15 tensors) is carried through, and
     mtp_num_hidden_layers is taken from the source config rather than
     pinned to zero.

     MTP runs at 5120 throughout and takes the same widening as the text
     path. mtp.fc reads a concatenation of embedding and hidden state, so
     both halves of its input are padded rather than only the tail.

